    <string name="notification_access_why">Latch looks for a date in them. When it finds one, it offers to turn that message into a calendar event or a to-do, so a date in a chat does not have to be retyped.</string>
    <string name="notification_access_memory">The text of a notification is read on this phone, in memory, and is never written to storage — not to Latch\'s Inbox, not to its queue, not anywhere else.</string>
